    rorExpectancy: 'Expectancy per trade',
    rorSimBasis: 'based on {n} Monte Carlo simulations',
    rorVerdictNegative: 'Negative expectancy: with these numbers ruin isn\'t a risk, it\'s a long-run mathematical certainty. Before tuning risk, you need a system with an edge.',
    rorVerdictHigh: 'The system has an edge, but risk per trade is too high — the probability of ruin is still serious. Lower the % per trade and watch it collapse.',
    rorVerdictOk: 'Solid combination: positive edge and controlled risk. Remember the simulation assumes perfect discipline — the stop is always honoured.',
    rorRecoveryTitle: 'Recovery math: what you lose vs. what you must gain back',
    rorNote: 'Simplified educational model: assumes independent trades, fixed compounded risk and no gaps/slippage. Reality is usually worse — treat it as a best case, not a promise.',
