    edu_fundamentosComprarVsVende_6227e3cc: 'Fundamentals: Buying vs Selling Options',
    edu_todaOperacionConOpciones_4b806806: 'Every options trade has TWO SIDES. The BUYER (Long) pays the premium and obtains a right. The SELLER (Short) collects the premium and accepts the obligation if exercised.',
    edu_lasGriegas_0ebfaf86: 'The Greeks',
    edu_lasGriegasCuantificanLa_560a7bae: 'The Greeks quantify the sensitivity of the premium to different factors. Mastering them is what separates the professional trader from the amateur.',
    edu_moneynessItmAtmOtm_a4a14296: 'Moneyness: ITM / ATM / OTM (explained)',
    edu_laMoneynessIndicaLa_d33c00c2: 'MONEYNESS indicates the relationship between the current price of the underlying (Spot S) and the Strike K. It defines the intrinsic value of the option and its behavior.',
    edu_volatilidadImplicitaIv_9566fdd4: 'Implied Volatility (IV)',
    edu_laIvEsEl_8e2ceb1e: 'IV is the market\'s price for future uncertainty. High IV makes premiums more expensive; low IV makes them cheaper. It is the MOST important factor after Delta.',
    edu_comoLeerElDiagrama_0e91a1f2: 'How to read the Payoff diagram',
    edu_elGraficoDePayoff_4228af6d: 'The payoff chart shows the PnL (Y-axis) as a function of the underlying\'s price at expiration (X-axis). The two key lines are T+0 (today) and At Expiry (expiration).',
    edu_longCallBuyCall_b69bddbc: 'LONG CALL (BUY CALL) → You pay premium. You profit if it rises > Strike+Premium. Maximum loss = premium paid.',
    edu_longPutBuyPut_0125f4de: 'LONG PUT (BUY PUT) → You pay premium. You profit if it falls < Strike−Premium. Maximum loss = premium paid.',
    edu_shortCallSellCall_46b9297a: 'SHORT CALL (SELL CALL) → You collect premium. You lose if it rises > Strike+Premium. Maximum loss = UNLIMITED (if naked).',
    edu_shortPutSellPut_cc28336a: 'SHORT PUT (SELL PUT) → You collect premium. You lose if it falls < Strike−Premium. Maximum loss = Strike−Premium if it drops to 0.',
    edu_regla802080_db62e282: '80/20 RULE → ~80% of options expire worthless → statistically the premium seller usually wins; but their risk/reward ratio is poor.',
    edu_deltaCambioEnPrima_0791393e: 'Delta Δ → Change in premium per $1 move in the underlying. Calls: 0 to +1. Puts: 0 to -1.',
    edu_thetaPerdidaDeValor_c24fe104: 'Theta Θ → Loss of time value per day that passes. Always negative for Long, positive for Short.',
    edu_vegaSensibilidadAlCambio_49f4d565: 'Vega ν → Sensitivity to change in implied volatility (IV). Positive for Long, negative for Short.',
    edu_gammaVelocidadDeCambio_2647e1e9: 'Gamma Γ → Rate of change of Delta; maximum near ATM. Longs: Positive Gamma. Shorts: Negative Gamma.',
    edu_rhoSensibilidadACambios_6dd807ab: 'Rho ρ → Sensitivity to changes in interest rates. Significant only for long-term options (LEAPS).',
    edu_call_094692fa: '── CALL ──',
    edu_itmInTheMoney_d20317a8: 'ITM (In-The-Money) → S > K. Has intrinsic value = S−K. Delta > 0.5. "Stock-like" behavior.',
    edu_atmAtTheMoney_638c9e7d: 'ATM (At-The-Money) → S ≈ K. No intrinsic value; only time value. Delta ≈ 0.5. Maximum Gamma and Vega.',
    edu_otmOutOfThe_2b67777e: 'OTM (Out-of-The-Money) → S < K. No intrinsic value; only time value. Delta < 0.5. Cheaper but riskier.',
    edu_put_a27fa8fc: '── PUT ──',
    edu_itmInTheMoney_bfd445a5: 'ITM (In-The-Money) → S < K. Has intrinsic value = K−S. Delta < −0.5.',
    edu_atmAtTheMoney_793be97c: 'ATM (At-The-Money) → S ≈ K. No intrinsic value; only time value. Delta ≈ −0.5.',
    edu_otmOutOfThe_71ddb79d: 'OTM (Out-of-The-Money) → S > K. No intrinsic value; only time value. Delta > −0.5.',
    edu_cLculoDelPayoff_2fb38b8e: '── PAYOFF CALCULATION AT EXPIRATION ──',
    edu_longCallPnlMax_e997a851: 'Long Call:  PnL = max(0, S−K) × 100 × contracts − premium_paid × 100',
    edu_longPutPnlMax_80f585a4: 'Long Put:   PnL = max(0, K−S) × 100 × contracts − premium_paid × 100',
    edu_shortCallPnlPrima_d573157a: 'Short Call: PnL = premium_received × 100 − max(0, S−K) × 100 × contracts',
    edu_shortPutPnlPrima_47fd35c2: 'Short Put:  PnL = premium_received × 100 − max(0, K−S) × 100 × contracts',
    edu_ivRankIvPercentile_da54acc4: 'IV Rank / IV Percentile → Contextualize current IV vs. historical (last 52 weeks).',
    edu_crushPostEarningsLa_c269719f: 'Post-earnings crush → IV collapses after the event; buyers often lose even when directionally correct.',
    edu_vegaLongVsShort_404de31c: 'Vega Long vs. Short → Buyers profit if IV rises; sellers if it falls.',
    edu_reglaPracticaComprarOpcio_98a9dbf8: 'Rule of thumb: BUY options with low IV (IV Rank < 30), SELL with high IV (IV Rank > 50).',
    edu_skewLasPutsOtm_02473640: 'Skew → OTM puts typically have higher IV than OTM calls (fear of downside).',
    edu_lineaVerdeCurrentP_ecfc0457: 'GREEN line (Current P&L) → Your theoretical PnL TODAY at different prices using Black-Scholes (includes time value).',
    edu_lineaBlancaPunteadaAt_8a5c4ef9: 'WHITE dotted line (At Expiry) → PnL IF you hold until expiration (no time value).',
    edu_lineaNaranjaSpotPrecio_de21f24f: 'ORANGE line (Spot) → Current underlying price. Main reference.',
    edu_lineaVioletaBreakEven_9112e631: 'VIOLET line (Break-Even) → Point where PnL = 0 at expiration. Above/below you profit.',
